+(** A numeral's own type (\secref{literals}), which exists only at compile
+    time: no numeral value exists when a program runs.  Its four numbers are
+    static parameters: the digit count %n%, the digits after the radix point
+    %m%, the radix %r%, and the digits read as one integer in that radix %v%.
+    A number type takes a numeral by a coercion generic over them, which reads
+    them as exact integers.  A numeral type is written only as the parameter
+    type of a coercion or an operator. **)
+trait Numeral extends Number end
+trait AnyNaturalNumeral extends Numeral excludes { AnyRadixPointNumeral } end
